<html lang="en">
<head><title>DB Assistant - Public LLM Chat</title></head>
<body style="${REGULAR_FONT_STYLE}">
<div style="${REGULAR_LARGE_FONT_STYLE}">
    <b>AI Assistant with Database Integration</b><br>
</div>
Get assistance with your database, workspace, and various coding tasks using natural language!<br><br>
DB Assistant is an AI-powered software development companion that seamlessly integrates with your workspace and database.<br>
It can help with a variety of tasks, such as providing insights into your database structure,
analyzing database code, identifying relevant code blocks, generating and optimizing SQL and PL/SQL code,
and assisting with any other programming language used in your workspace.

<br>
<br>
<br>
<u>Before You Begin</u><br><br>
To start using DB Assistant, ensure the following prerequisites are met:
<ul>
    <li><b>Network Access</b> - Configure your network settings to enable secure communication with your chosen LLM provider’s API endpoint (System Settings > HTTP Proxy).</li>
    <li><b>API Credentials</b> - Enter your API keys for the selected LLM provider (e.g., OpenAI, Cohere, Anthropic, or other supported public APIs).</li>
    <li><b>AI Profiles</b> - Create custom AI profiles to tailor the language model’s behavior, such as adjusting the balance between objectivity and creativity or adding specific instructions.</li>
</ul>
For detailed setup guidance, refer to the Oracle® Database Navigator documentation.

<br>
<br>
<br>
<b>NOTE</b><br>
This is an experimental feature. Output accuracy may vary depending on the selected language model, your database access permissions, and other factors.
Validate outputs carefully and report any issues to the Oracle® Database Navigator development team to help improve this feature.
</body>
</html>